          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Political Vision</strong><br>\nBeyond military conquests, Bolivar had a grand vision for a united South America, often referred to as \"Gran Colombia.\" He sought to create a federation of states in the region, with democratic governance as its foundation.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Challenges and Obstacles</strong><br>\nBolivar's attempts to unify the continent faced immense challenges, including geographical barriers, regional rivalries, and political dissent. His dream of a united Latin America was difficult to maintain due to the emerging political and social divisions.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Presidency and Governance</strong><br>\nIn the territories he helped liberate, Bolivar took on leadership roles, including the presidency of Gran Colombia. His governance was marked by efforts to implement reforms that would create a modern, cohesive state.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
