            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Later Years and Resignation</strong><br>\nBolivar's later years saw his vision undermined by political turmoil and dissent within his own ranks. Disheartened, he resigned his presidency in 1830, expressing despair over the region's internal conflicts.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Legacy</strong><br>\nBolivar died on December 17, 1830, in Santa Marta, Colombia, from tuberculosis. Despite his dream for unity not being realized in his lifetime, he is remembered as a symbol of liberation and a key figure in Latin American history.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Lasting Impact</strong><br>\nSimon Bolivar's legacy lives on in the countries he helped found. His name and ideals continue to inspire people fighting for freedom and justice in Latin America and around the world.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
